diff --git a/.audit/j2k-reset.tsv b/.audit/j2k-reset.tsv
index 09c96a416d591ae2c6fa2761a8afa73b38a113d2..29435685c8d810106bb29f48076df688bd06e9d1 100644
--- a/.audit/j2k-reset.tsv
+++ b/.audit/j2k-reset.tsv
@@ -35,3 +35,10 @@ ts	phase	decision	why	evidence	result
 2026-08-20T20:08:00Z	review	closed the independent novel-statistics audit	separated fallible analysis from persistence and added explicit unspaced-script segmentation after two review rounds found reader-availability and CJK/Thai undercount risks	NovelTextStatistics.kt; NovelReaderSession.kt	VERIFIED
 2026-08-20T20:10:00Z	validation	ran the complete novel suite plus legacy extension compatibility before final review fixes	verified the statistics integration did not regress reader, formats, downloads, quotes, or installed-novel linkage	gradlew :app:testDevDebugUnitTest --tests dev.ahmedmohamed.hayai.novel.* --tests eu.kanade.tachiyomi.source.NovelSourceCompatibilityTest	VERIFIED
 2026-08-20T20:14:00Z	validation	reran focused statistics tests after the final review fixes	verified analysis and DB failure fallback plus Chinese, Thai, Korean, and Japanese segmentation in the final code	gradlew :app:testDevDebugUnitTest --tests dev.ahmedmohamed.hayai.novel.statistics.*	VERIFIED
+2026-08-20T21:10:00Z	novel-plugins	built end-to-end LNReader-compatible repository sources	added explicit repository trust, bounded catalogs and downloads, atomic integrity-checked installs, isolated QuickJS runtimes, catalogue/chapter adapters, source registration, missing-source names, management UI, and backup/restore	app/src/main/java/dev/ahmedmohamed/hayai/novel/plugin	IMPLEMENTED
+2026-08-20T21:18:00Z	validation	compiled the integrated runtime and ran focused plugin contract tests	verified descriptor validation, relative URLs, stable IDs, semantic versions, resource wiring, and J2K source integration	gradlew :app:compileDevDebugKotlin :app:testDevDebugUnitTest --tests dev.ahmedmohamed.hayai.novel.plugin.*	VERIFIED
+2026-08-20T21:42:00Z	review	closed the first independent JavaScript plugin audit	added authenticated relative asset loading, plugin setting backup, live restore reload, and off-main UI schema preparation after review found four integration gaps	NovelPluginSource.kt; NovelPluginManager.kt; HayaiBackupService.kt	IMPLEMENTED
+2026-08-20T21:49:00Z	validation	fixed bounded stream accounting after the focused compiler rejected an integer width mismatch	kept the byte budget as a Long across reads and skips	NovelPluginSource.kt:1596	VERIFIED
+2026-08-20T21:53:00Z	validation	compiled the plugin integration and ran focused plugin and backup tests	verified source registration, runtime contracts, protobuf compatibility, plugin code and settings round trips, and restore limits	gradlew :app:compileDevDebugKotlin; gradlew :app:testDevDebugUnitTest --tests dev.ahmedmohamed.hayai.novel.plugin.* --tests dev.ahmedmohamed.hayai.backup.*	VERIFIED
+2026-08-20T22:16:00Z	review	closed the second independent JavaScript plugin audit	routed restore through runtime preflight and kept previous code, metadata, settings, and live runtimes intact until replacement publication	NovelPluginManager.kt; NovelPluginStore.kt; HayaiBackupService.kt	VERIFIED
+2026-08-20T22:19:00Z	validation	reran focused plugin and backup tests after transactional restore fixes	verified the final suspend restore integration, plugin contracts, backup protobuf limits, and chapter asset URL cases	gradlew :app:testDevDebugUnitTest --tests dev.ahmedmohamed.hayai.novel.plugin.* --tests dev.ahmedmohamed.hayai.backup.*	VERIFIED
